{
  "id": "lib-json-variables",
  "order": 2,
  "title": "Formula variables and math of the library",
  "goal": "Port the library's `json/variable` (the variables a formula can read: the level, the entity's health, a tool stat, a modifier's data), `json/math` and `json/field` classes on top of the existing `PostFixFormula` (src/formula.rs). A variable is a struct with `from_json` and a `get` over a context trait; the same variable loader table the original has is a map from type id to loader. This is what lets `attribute`, `protection` and the conditional modules leave raw data.",
